        <item>
            <title>2.25.0</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 10:40:44 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>107</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.25.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Features

- **Canopy Mobile** — a companion iPhone app. Every Mac running Canopy publishes its panes to a relay, so one phone shows every session on every machine: what each is doing, how much context it has left, and how long it has been in that state.
- **Reply from the phone.** A session's notification opens that session's conversation, and what you type is injected as a real user turn — not a note, not a queue.
- **Answer permission requests from the phone** — Allow, Deny, or Always, from the lock screen or the app. Always writes the rule the CLI itself proposed, so a decision made on the phone is byte-for-byte the one the desktop button would have written. The Mac's prompt retracts when the phone answers it.
- **Notification history.** A push that arrives while the phone is locked and is never tapped is still recorded, so nothing that finished overnight is lost. Bodies render as Markdown; a shell command scrolls rather than wrapping.

### Changes

- Completion notifications now carry the assistant's own final message instead of a generic line.
- Preferences split into six tabs — General keeps only the small toggles, with MacroPad and Mobile getting their own.
- A session's notifications stay grouped across a Canopy restart.

### Bug Fixes

- Notification bodies are truncated by UTF-8 bytes rather than characters, so a Japanese or emoji-heavy completion is no longer silently dropped by APNs for exceeding its 4 KB payload limit.
]]></description>
